gpc:30014506 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "MORTADELLA"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Mortadella is a large Italian-type sausage or cold cut sausage made of finely hashed/ground heat-cured pork, which incorporates at least 15% small cubes of pork fat (principally the hard fat from the neck of the pig). It is delicately flavored with spices, including whole or ground black pepper, myrtle berries, nutmeg, coriander and pistachios and/or olives. In several Arab and Muslim countries, Mortadella is made from chicken, beef, or turkey."@en .

gpc:30014507 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "WIENER/VIENNA/FRANKFURTER (WURSTEL)/HOT DOG"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A moist sausage of soft, even texture and flavor, often made from mechanically recovered meat or meat slurry. Most types are cured or sometimes smoked and may have the casing removed after the cooking process. Hot dogs are sold fully cooked and ready to eat, although they are usually warmed before serving."@en .

gpc:30014508 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BLOOD SAUSAGE/BLACK PUDDING/BLOOD PUDDING"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Blood sausage is made by cooking blood with a filler until it is thick enough to congeal when cooled. Typical fillers include meat, fat, suet, bread, sweet potato, barley and oatmeal, and different meat sources are used."@en .

gpc:30014509 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "LIVERWURST/LIVER SAUSAGE/BRAUNSWEIGER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Liverwurst is a sausage containing about 10 to 20% liver, which gives a distinctive liver taste. Other ingredients are meat, fat, and spices such as ground black pepper, marjoram, allspice, thyme, ground mustard or nutmeg. Most liverwurst varieties are spreadable. Liverwurst is sold ready to eat, but it can be cooked further as well."@en .

gpc:30014510 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "EXTRAWURST"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Extrawurst is an finely emulsified sausage, commonly of Austrian or German origin, with added bacon, garlic, spices and often potato added as a starch. It is cooked and served cold."@en .

gpc:30014511 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "MERGUEZ"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Merguez is a red, spicy sausage from Algeria and Tunisia, North Africa. Merguez is flavoured with a wide range of spices, such as sumac for tartness, and paprika, cayenne pepper, or harissa, a hot chili paste, that gives it a red color. It is traditionally made fresh and eaten after grilling."@en .

gpc:30014512 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "MET(T)WURST"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Mettwurst is a strongly flavoured German sausage made from raw minced meat, which is preserved by curing and smoking. The most common variety is soft and somewhat smoked but still soft and spreadable."@en .

gpc:30014514 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BRATWURST"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Bratwurst is a sausage composed of several kinds of finely chopped meat that is traditionally prepared by grilling."@en .

gpc:30014515 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CHORIZO/CHOURICO/LONGANIZA"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Chorizo is typically a fermented, cured, smoked sausage that has a distinctive smokiness and deep red color from dried, smoked red peppers. Chorizo originates from the Iberian Peninsula."@en .

gpc:30014516 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "WEISSWURST"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Weisswurst is a traditional Bavarian sausage made from very finely minced meat and fresh bacon. It is an unsmoked sausage usually flavoured with parsley, lemon, mace, onions, ginger and cardamom. For consumption, the sausages are quickly boiled in water, resulting in a greyish-white colour when served."@en .

gpc:30014517 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CERVELAT"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Cervelat is a cooked sausage consisting of a mixture of different meat, bacon, and pork rind that is packed into zebu intestines, slightly smoked and then boiled. It is produced mainly in Switzerland and in parts of Germany."@en .

gpc:30014518 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BIERSCHINKEN/KRAKAUER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Bierschinken is a scalded sausage from a cured mixture of meat, lard and spices that incorporates at least 15% small cubes of pork fat or cooked ham. It is produced mainly in Germany and Austria."@en .

gpc:30014519 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "TEEWURST"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Teewurst is a German sausage made from two parts of raw pork (and sometimes beef) and one part bacon, which are minced, seasoned, and typically packed in porous, artificial casings before being smoked over beech wood. The sausage is then aged for seven to ten days in order to develop its typical taste. Teewurst contains 30 to 40 percent fat, which makes it particularly easy to spread."@en .

gpc:30014520 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BOLOGNA"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Bologna is an American-style sausage similar to Italian mortadella that can be made out of either chicken, turkey, beef, or pork. It is finely chopped or ground and contains lard, but without any visible pieces of fat. It is packed into casings with a variety of shapes including ring, chub, loaf, or rope. It is cooked, sometimes smoked, and sold with the casing removed and ready to eat."@en .

gpc:30014521 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "COUNTRY/BREAKFAST"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Country and breakfast sausage is made from whole muscle product that is fresh and not cured or smoked (also known as &quot;Whole Hog&quot; sausage). It is normally made from pork but sometimes from turkey or beef. It is chopped and packed into casings for links or shaped as patties and used as part of a traditional American breakfast cuisine."@en .

gpc:30014522 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "ITALIAN SAUSAGE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A popular American-style sausage with traditional flavors and spices of Italy (fennel and/or anise). It is typically made from pork but sometimes from turkey or beef. Normally it is fresh but can be smoked. It is chopped and packed into casings for links, shaped as patties, or sold in loose bulk and used for stuffing, fillings and meat balls."@en .

gpc:30014523 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "KIELBASA"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A traditional seasoned and gently smoked Polish sausage made from choice cuts of pork, and often mixed with a little beef or veal."@en .

gpc:30014524 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "LINGUICA"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A Portuguese-style cured pork sausage seasoned with onions, garlic, and paprika."@en .

gpc:30014525 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "KNOCKWURST"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A short, plump sausage made from ground veal and pork with fresh garlic in hog casings. Aged over burning oak wood."@en .

gpc:30014526 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "THURINGER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A sausage from the German state of Thuringia made from finely minced pork, beef, or veal. It is seasoned with salt, pepper, caraway, marjoram, and garlic. Normally it is smoked and cured."@en .

gpc:30014527 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "ANDOUILLE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A spiced, heavily smoked pork sausage, distinguished in some varieties by its use of the entire gastrointestinal system of the pig."@en .

gpc:30014528 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BOCKWURST"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A German-style sausage made from ground veal and pork, flavored with salt, white pepper and paprika."@en .

gpc:30014529 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BOEREWORS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Boerewors is a South African sausage made from coarsely minced beef, sometimes combined with minced pork, lamb, or both and spices such as coriander seed, black pepper, nutmeg, cloves and allspice. The sausage is preserved with salt and vinegar and packed in sausage casings. Traditional boerewors is usually formed into a continuous spiral. It can also be dried into what is colloquially known as droe wors."@en .

