gpc:30015575 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "WAXY"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Low to medium starch/high to medium moisture potatoes. Ideally suited for potato salad, stewing, firm boiled potatoes; jacket potatoes and fried potatoes, gratin, and fritters. The term waxy is subjective. The supplier of the potatoes ultimately determines the cooking type."@en .

gpc:30015576 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PREDOMINANTLY WAXY"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Lower starch potatoes than waxy and absorb less water when cooked. These are usually new or young potatoes. They can have a dry matter of 14% or less but that is subjective. The supplier of the potatoes ultimately determines the cooking type. Ideal for boiled and jacket potatoes, as well as fried and grilled potatoes, stews, casseroles, soups, and fritters."@en .

gpc:30015577 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "FLOURY"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "High starch/low moisture potatoes are also described as having high solids. Also referred to as Creamy. They have a dry matter (starch content) of 22% or greater. In some varieties based on climate this amount starts at 26% dry matter. Ideal for jacket and boiled potatoes, mashed potatoes, dumplings, stews and soups."@en .

gpc:30015578 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
