  rdfs:label "BEETROOT LEAVES"@en .

gpc:30016219 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SWISS CHARD"@en .

gpc:30016220 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BABY CABBAGE LEAVES"@en .

gpc:30016221 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "WILD CRANBERRY"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Grown from Vaccinium oxycoccos or Oxycoccus palustris."@en .

gpc:30016222 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CRANBERRY"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Cranberries of Vaccinium macrocarpon or Oxycoccus macrocarpus ."@en .

gpc:30016223 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BRAZILIAN CHERRY"@en .

gpc:30016224 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "JAMBULAN"@en .

gpc:30016225 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "MALABAR PLUM"@en .

gpc:30016226 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "DJAMBOEAJER"@en .

gpc:30016227 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PORTUGUESE KALE"@en .

gpc:30016228 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SIBERIAN KALE"@en .

gpc:30016229 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "COMMON KALE"@en .

gpc:30016230 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PERENNIAL KALE"@en .

gpc:30016233 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "FIGATELLI"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Figatelli Sausage is a long, thin, highly flavored smoked pork liver sausage from Corsica."@en .

gpc:30016234 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PERRENIAL"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Products who lifespan is typically for more than 2 years."@en .

gpc:30016235 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "FLOWERING"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Plant products that derive their decorative purpose from their beatifull coloured flowers."@en .

gpc:30016236 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "FOLIAGE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Plant products that derive their decorative purpose from their specticular coloured leaves or leaf-form."@en .

gpc:30016237 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BUTTERMILK POWDER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Used in the production of ice cream as a source of solids, in processed sliced cheese to increase viscosity, as an emulsifier in chocolate products and in dry mixes such as pancake mix, to add dairy flavor and enhance food browning."@en .

gpc:30016238 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CASEIN"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The name for a family of related phosphoproteins (&#945;S1, &#945;S2, &#946;, &#954;). These proteins are commonly found in mammalian milk, making up 80% of the proteins incow milk and between 20% and 45% of the proteins in human milk."@en .

gpc:30016239 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "MILK SKIN"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A sticky film of protein that forms on top of milk and milk-containing liquids (such as hot chocolate and some soups). It is caused by the denaturation of proteins such as casein."@en .

gpc:30016240 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "VACCENIC ACID"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "An omega-7 fatty acid. It is a naturally occurring trans-fatty acid found in the fat of ruminants and in dairy products such as milk, butter, and yogurt."@en .

gpc:30016241 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "WHEY"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The liquid remaining after milk has been curdled and strained. It is a by-product of the manufacture of cheese or casein and has several commercial uses."@en .

gpc:30016242 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "WHEY PROTEIN"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A mixture of globular proteins isolated from whey, the liquid material created as a by-product of cheese production."@en .

gpc:30016243 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "EGG PRODUCT"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe those products where egg products are the key ingrediate such as an omelette."@en .

gpc:30016244 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SUSHI"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term, Sushi, is used to describe a Japanese food consisting of cooked vinegared rice combined with other ingredients, usually raw fish or other seafood."@en .

gpc:30016245 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "TOFU"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe those products where tofu, also known as bean curd, which is made by coagulating soy milk, is the key ingrediate."@en .

gpc:30016246 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "UNFLAVOURED"@en .

gpc:30016247 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "DISPOSABLE ELECTRONIC CIGARETTE"@en .

gpc:30016248 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "RECHARGEABLE ELECTRONIC CIGARETTE"@en .

gpc:30016249 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "ELECTRONIC CIGARETTE REPLACEMENT CARTRIDGES"@en .

gpc:30016250 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "ELECTRONIC CIGARETTE BATTERIES"@en .

gpc:30016251 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "ELECTRONIC CIGARETTE BATTERY CHARGER"@en .

gpc:30016252 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "ELECTRONIC CIGARETTE CARRYING CASE"@en .

gpc:30016253 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "ELECTRONIC CIGARETTE KIT"@en .

gpc:30016254 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BUTCHER BLOCK"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Edge grain butcher block tops have parallel wood rails that run the length of the piece. End grain butcher block tops are created by fusing together the end pieces of wood rails into a checkerboard pattern."@en .

gpc:30016255 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "COMPRESSED PAPER OR FIBRE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Paper composite countertops are made of post-consumer recycled paper and other fibers held together by a formaldehyde-free thermoset plastic resin. Available in thicknesses ranging from 1 inch to 2 inches."@en .

gpc:30016256 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CONCRETE- CAST IN PLACE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A composite material composed of coarse granular material (the aggregate or filler) embedded in a hard matrix of material (the cement or binder) that fills the space among the aggregate particles and glues them together. This product is cast at the installation site."@en .

gpc:30016257 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CONCRETE- PRECAST"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A construction product produced by casting concrete in a reusable mold or &quot;form&quot; which is then cured in a controlled environment, transported to the construction site and put into place."@en .

gpc:30016258 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "GABBRO"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A large group of dark, coarse-grained, intrusive mafic igneous rocks chemically equivalent to basalt."@en .

gpc:30016259 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "GLASS- CRAFTED"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Glass of various colours, hues and shapes which have been moulded together for use."@en .

gpc:30016260 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "GLASS - RECYCLED"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Glass which as been recylced from other uses and crushed or refired for purposes of subsequent use."@en .

gpc:30016261 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "HIGH-DENSITY POLYTHYLENE (HDPE) - RECYCLED"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "High-Density Polyethylene (HDPE) which as been recylced from other uses and refired for purposes of subsequent use."@en .

gpc:30016262 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "LAVA"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Volcanic lava stone is extracted by hand from open-air quarries, then cut into slabs, glazed with enamel, and fired in a kiln at 1300 degrees. During cooling a smooth crackled finish develops."@en .

gpc:30016263 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "MELAMINE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "An organic base and a trimer of cyanamide, with a 1,3,5-triazine skeleton."@en .

gpc:30016264 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PALM WOOD"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Arecaceae or are a botanical family of perennial lianas, shrubs, and trees commonly known as palm trees."@en .

gpc:30016265 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "QUARTZ- ENGINEERED"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Quartz countertops are man-made engineered stone countertops formed by combining 90% ground quartz (a natural hard mineral) with 8-10% resins, polymers, and pigments. This forms a very hard granite-like surface. The appearance depends on how the quartz is ground: coarsely ground quartz produces a flecked appearance, while finely ground quartz produces a smooth look."@en .

gpc:30016266 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SOAPSTONE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Soapstone is a natural stone, like granite, that is quarried. It&apos;s composed mostly of mineral talc, which makes it quite soft, but soapstone used for countertops typically has higher percentages of quartz in it, which makes it harder and more suitable as a kitchen surface."@en .

gpc:30016267 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SOLID SURFACES MATERIALS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Synthetic or manufactured solid surface countertops are made of man-made materials, most often acrylic, but also polyester resins, marble dust, and other pigments."@en .

gpc:30016268 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "TERRAZZO"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A composite material, poured in place or precast, consisting of marble, quartz, granite, glass, or other suitable chips, sprinkled or unsprinkled, and poured with a binder that is cementitious, chemical, or a combination of both. Terrazzo is cured and then ground and polished to a smooth surface or otherwise finished to produce a uniformly textured surface."@en .

gpc:30016269 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "TILE- CERAMIC"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Ceramic tile is made from clay, which is fired at a high temperature."@en .

gpc:30016270 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "TILE- GLASS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Pieces of glass formed into consistent shapes."@en .

gpc:30016271 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "TILE- NATURAL STONE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Pieces of stone formed into consistent shapes as opposed to cut from large slabs."@en .

gpc:30016272 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "TRAVERTINE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A form of limestone deposited by mineral springs, especially hot springs. Travertine often has a fibrous or concentric appearance and exists in white, tan, and cream-colored varieties."@en .

gpc:30016273 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "WOOD- RECLAIMED"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Processed wood retrieved from its original application for purposes of subsequent use."@en .

gpc:30016274 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "ZINC"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Zinc bears a dull, slightly mottled surface that has more in common with pewter than with chrome or stainless steel. It looks seasoned even when it&apos;s new, and it has an inherent warmth that many metals lack."@en .

gpc:30016275 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "GLAZED"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The item has been finished with a glaze to provide a lustrous or glassy appearance. This finish may or may not be fired in a kiln, depending on the material to which it is applied."@en .

gpc:30016276 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "UNGLAZED"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The item has not been finished with a glaze to provide a lustrous or glassy appearance."@en .

gpc:30016277 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BRUSHED"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The item has been finished with a process whereby marks on the surface either from sanding, as in metal surfaces, or by bristle marks, as in painted or finished surfaces."@en .

gpc:30016278 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "FLAMED"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The item has been finished with a process whereby the item was subjected to flames or fire to provide a scorched or burned look."@en .

gpc:30016279 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "POLISHED"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The item has been finished with a process whereby the item was ground and buffed typically with machines and polishing compounds."@en .

gpc:30016280 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "COMBINATION FINISH"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The item has been finished using a combination of several different finishing methods such as, but not limited to Polishing, Flaming, Glazing, or Oil Rubbing."@en .

gpc:30016281 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SATIN"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The finish of the item has an optical property on the surface of a extremely low to no-luster sheen, although it is not as dull as a Matte finish. (25-35% gloss)"@en .

gpc:30016282 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "ANTIQUE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The item has been finished with a process whereby the item has been painted, glazed, dinged, pitted, rubbed, or otherwise made to show wear and use patterns. These patterns provide the impression that the item is older than it is."@en .

gpc:30016283 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "DRYING OILS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The item has been finished with a process whereby the item was rubbed with oils such linseed or tugsten oil, parafin or beeswax."@en .

gpc:30016284 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BATHROOM/ VANITY"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe products the manufacturer has specifically designed for use in a room often called a bathroom, lavatory, restroom, toilet, water closet or on a cabinet called a vanity."@en .

gpc:30016285 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "GARAGE/ WORKSHOP"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe products the manufacturer has specifically designed for use in a room or area often called a garage, carport, workshop, or toolshed."@en .

gpc:30016286 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "OFFICE/ WORK STATION"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe products the manufacturer has specifically designed for use in a room often called an office, or work station."@en .

gpc:30016287 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CONCRETE- PROCESSED SLABS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A common structural element of slabs of steel reinforced concrete."@en .

gpc:30016288 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "WHISK"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe an attachment used to whisk semi-solids and liquids so as to combine ingredients and introduce air into the mixture."@en .

gpc:30016289 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BREAD HOOKS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe an attachment used to knead ingredients in a dough for bread or similar items."@en .

gpc:30016290 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BEATERS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe an attachment used to beat or mix ingredients."@en .

gpc:30016291 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "LIQUID BEATER ROD"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe an attachment used to combine liquid ingredients and introduce air into the mixture."@en .

gpc:30016292 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "RACK/HANGER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a carrier or hook which suspends an item in the cook area."@en .

gpc:30016293 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PHYSICAL ACTIVITY MONITOR"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe those products which are multi-feature devices used to track and monitor personal fitness."@en .

gpc:30016294 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "AMARANTH OIL"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe those oil products that are made from Amaranth oil which is extracted from the seeds of two species of the genus Amaranthus , that are called, collectively, grain amaranth. Amaranth oil is a light to medium colored, is pourable at low temperatures, and is highly unsaturated."@en .

gpc:30016295 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "LINSEED/FLAXSEED OIL"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe those food-grade oil products that are a colourless to yellowish oil obtained from the dried, ripened seeds of the flax plant ( Linum usitatissimum, Linaceae ).&#160;"@en .

gpc:30016296 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PUMPKIN SEED OIL"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe those oil products that are made from pumpkins grown primarily from Cucurbita pepo or Cucurbita moschata .&#160;"@en .

gpc:30016297 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SEA BUCKTHORN OIL"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe those oil products that made from Sea-buckthorn seeds or fruit pulp. Sea buckthorn is of the genus Hippophae . &#160;The most commonly used is Hippophae rhamnoides .&#160;"@en .

gpc:30016298 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "NAIL TOP COAT"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Nail Top Coat indicates the descriptive term used by the product manufacturer to identify the type of nail polish that is a clear coloured polish formula that is used specifically after applying nail polish to the nail. It forms a hardened barrier for the nail that can prevent chipping, scratching and peeling. Many top coats are marketed as &quot;quick-drying&quot; and/or helping the underlying polish to dry quickly."@en .

gpc:30016299 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SUGAR LOAF"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A tall cone of pressed sugar with a rounded top."@en .

gpc:30016300 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "RICE BASED CHIPS/CRISPS"@en .

gpc:30016301 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CHIPS BASED FROM POTATO POWDER"@en .

gpc:30016302 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "MIXED MEAT/POULTRY"@en .

gpc:30016303 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "NO MEAT"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This item contains no meat."@en .

gpc:30016304 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "NO FISH"@en .

gpc:30016305 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "NO SHELLFISH"@en .

gpc:30016306 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "COLOURING/PAINTING"@en .

gpc:30016307 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "STICKERS"@en .

gpc:30016308 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "TACTILE"@en .

gpc:30016309 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CONDENSED MILK"@en .

gpc:30016310 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "MILD (900-1999 SCOVILLE)"@en .

gpc:30016311 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "MEDIUM (2000-19.999 SCOVILLE)"@en .

gpc:30016312 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "HOT (20.000-100.000 SCOVILLE)"@en .

gpc:30016313 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "EXTRA HOT (&gt; 100.000 SCOVILLE)"@en .

gpc:30016314 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "ANCHO"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term describes the Ancho Chili Pepper, a variety of the species Capsicum annuum , to be supplied fresh."@en .

gpc:30016315 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BIRD&apos;S EYE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term describes the Bird&apos;s eye Chili Pepper, a variety of the species Capsicum annuum , to be supplied fresh."@en .

gpc:30016316 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CAPSICUM BACCATUM"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term describes the species Capsicum Baccatum , to be supplied fresh."@en .

gpc:30016317 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CHERRY CHILI PEPPER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term describes the Cherry Chili Pepper, a variety of the species Capsicum annuum , to be supplied fresh."@en .

gpc:30016318 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "DORSET NAGA"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term describes the Dorset naga Chili Pepper, a substrain of the original Naga, selected from the Bangladeshi varieties of the chili, naga morich , to be supplied fresh."@en .

gpc:30016319 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "FATALII"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term describes the Fatalii Chili Pepper, a variety of the species Capsicum chinense , to be supplied fresh."@en .

gpc:30016320 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "FRESNO"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term describes the Fresno Chili Pepper, a variety of the species Capsicum annuum , to be supplied fresh."@en .

gpc:30016321 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "HABANERO"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term describes the Habanero Chili Pepper, a variety of the species Capsicum chinense , to be supplied fresh."@en .

gpc:30016322 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "MADAME JEANETTE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term describes the Madame Jeanette Chili Pepper, a variety of the species Capsicum chinense , to be supplied fresh."@en .

gpc:30016323 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "MANZANO"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term describes the Manzano Chili Pepper of the species Capsicum pubescens , to be supplied fresh."@en .

gpc:30016324 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "NAGA JOLOKIA"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term describes the Naga jolokia Chili Pepper, &#160;an interspecies hybrid, mostly Capsicum chinense with some Capsicum frutescens genes, to be supplied fresh."@en .

gpc:30016325 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "NAGA VIPER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term describes the Naga viper Chili Pepper, &#160;an unstable three-way hybrid produced from the Naga Morich, the Naga Jolokia and the Trinidad Scorpion , to be supplied fresh."@en .

gpc:30016326 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PASILLA"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term describes the Pasilla Chili Pepper, a variety of the species Capsicum annuum , to be supplied fresh."@en .

gpc:30016327 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PIQUIN"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term describes the Piquin Chili Pepper, a variety&#160; glabriusculum&#160; of the species Capsicum annuum , to be supplied fresh."@en .

gpc:30016328 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "POBLANO"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term describes the Poblano Chili Pepper, a variety of the species Capsicum annuum , to be supplied fresh."@en .

gpc:30016329 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PRIK-CHEE-FAH"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term describes the Prik-chee-fah Chili Pepper, a variety of the species Capsicum annuum , to be supplied fresh."@en .

gpc:30016330 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SCOTCH BONNET"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term describes the Scotch Bonnet Chili Pepper, a variety of the species Capsicum chinense , to be supplied fresh."@en .

gpc:30016331 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SERRANO"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term describes the Serrano Chili Pepper, a variety of the species Capsicum annuum , to be supplied fresh."@en .

gpc:30016332 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "TABASCO"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term describes the Tabasco Chili Pepper, a variety of the species Capsicum frutescens , to be supplied fresh."@en .

gpc:30016333 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "TRINIDAD SCORPION"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term describes the Trinidad scorpion Chili Pepper, a variety of the species Capsicum chinense , to be supplied fresh."@en .

gpc:30016334 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "X&apos;CATIK"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term describes the X&apos;catik Chili Pepper, a variety of the species Capsicum annuum , to be supplied fresh."@en .

gpc:30016335 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CONFERENCE"@en .

gpc:30016336 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "YOUNG ADULT"@en .

gpc:30016337 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PLAYSTATION 4"@en .

gpc:30016338 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PLAYSTATION VITA"@en .

gpc:30016339 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "NINTENDO WII U"@en .

gpc:30016340 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "NINTENDO 3DS"@en .

gpc:30016341 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "XBOX ONE"@en .

gpc:30016342 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "OUYA"@en .

gpc:30016343 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PANEL CURTAIN"@en .

gpc:30016344 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "ROLLER BLIND"@en .

gpc:30016345 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "ROMAN BLIND"@en .

gpc:30016346 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "VERTICAL BLIND"@en .

gpc:30016347 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "VENETIAN BLIND / HORIZONTAL BLIND"@en .

gpc:30016348 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "TOY BALL"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Indicates, with reference to the product branding, labelling or packaging, the descriptive term that is used by the product manufacturer to identify that includes any ball that is not designed for use in a specific sport, but designed for young children to play with. Typically has licensed designs or characters printed on it. Excludes any balls with a designated sport purpose, such as a football, basketball golf ball etc."@en .

