gpc:30016372 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "KOSHU"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Koshu is a white wine grape variety that has been grown primarily in Yamanashi Prefecture of Japan."@en .

gpc:30016373 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "NIAGARA"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Niagara grapes are a variety of the North American grape species Vitis labrusca and are used as table grapes and for wines, as well as jams and juice.&#160;"@en .

gpc:30016374 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "RYUGAN"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Ryugan (also known as Senkoji, possibly the same as China&apos;s Longyan), is grown in small quantities, predominantly in Nagano Prefecture in central Honshu."@en .

gpc:30016375 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BLACK QUEEN"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Black Queen is a Japanese hybrid grape variety,"@en .

gpc:30016376 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "DELAWARE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "The Delaware grape is a cultivar derived from the grape species Vitis Labrusca or &apos;Fox Grape&apos; which is used for the table and wine production."@en .

gpc:30016377 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "MUSCAT BAILEY A"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Muscat Bailey A is a red wine grape hybrid developed by Zenbei Kawakami (1868-1944) at the Iwanohara Winery in Niigata Prefecture."@en .

