gpc:30018058 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SALT BOX"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container with or without a lid, intended for the storage of kitchen salt.&#160;"@en .

gpc:30018059 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SPICE BOX"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container with or without a lid intended for the storage of spices such as oregano, thyme etc. Typically this product has more than one compartment to hold the spices."@en .

gpc:30018060 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "LID HOLDER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a storage device for holding lids of kitchen utensils. Can be hung or placed on the work surface or put in a drawer."@en .

gpc:30018061 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SINGLE HOOK FOR UTENSILS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe an object (made of metal or any other material), with a curved extremity from which kitchen utensils such as spoons and ladles can be suspended."@en .

gpc:30018062 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BLINI MOLD (NON DISPOSABLE)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a mold used to shape blinis."@en .

gpc:30018063 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BORDELAIS FLUTED CAKE MOLDS (NON DISPOSABLE)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of non disposable mold used for the cooking of Bordeaux fluted cakes."@en .

gpc:30018064 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BRIOCHE MOLD (NON DISPOSABLE)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of non-disposable mold used for the cooking of brioche."@en .

gpc:30018065 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CREME BRULEE DISH (NON DISPOSABLE)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a cooking dish used for cooking and serving creme brulee."@en .

gpc:30018066 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "FINANCIER MOLD (NON DISPOSABLE)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of non-disposable mold used for the cooking of financier cakes."@en .

gpc:30018067 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "INDIVIDUAL BRIOCHE MOLD (NON DISPOSABLE)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of non disposable mold used for the cooking of individual brioche."@en .

gpc:30018068 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "KOUGLOFF MOLD (NON DISPOSABLE)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of non-disposable mold used for the cooking of gugelhupf cakes."@en .

gpc:30018069 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "LASAGNA DISH (NON DISPOSABLE)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a rectangular-shaped cooking recipient, with high sides, intended for the cooking in the oven of lasagne-style pasta dishes."@en .

gpc:30018070 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "MADELEINE MOULD (NON DISPOSABLE)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of non-disposable mold used for the cooking of madeleine cakes."@en .

gpc:30018071 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "MINI FONDUE DISH (NON DISPOSABLE)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a small cooking casserole-style utensil, usually earthenware or cast iron, with a handle for the preparation and serving of individual portions."@en .

gpc:30018072 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "MINI-BORDELAIS FLUTED CAKE MOLD (NON DISPOSABLE)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of non-disposable mold used for the cooking of mini-rectangular cakes."@en .

gpc:30018073 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "MINI-MADELEINE MOLD (NON DISPOSABLE)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of non-disposable mold used for the cooking of mini-madeleine cakes."@en .

gpc:30018074 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "MINI-RECTANGULAR CAKE MOLD (NON DISPOSABLE)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a rather deep mold intended for the cooking of mini-rectangular cakes."@en .

gpc:30018075 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "MUFFINS MOLD (NON DISPOSABLE)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of non-disposable mold used for the cooking of muffins."@en .

gpc:30018076 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PETITS FOURS MOLD (NON DISPOSABLE)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of non-disposable mold used for the cooking of petits fours."@en .

gpc:30018077 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PYRAMID MOLD (NON DISPOSABLE)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a mold used for the cooking of cakes to give them shape of a pyramid."@en .

gpc:30018078 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "RAMEKIN"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a small bowl used for cooking and serving individual portion of various dishes."@en .

gpc:30018079 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "RAVIOLIS MOLD"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a mold used to shape ravioli."@en .

gpc:30018080 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "ROUND CHARLOTTE MOLD (NON DISPOSABLE)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of non-disposable mold used for the cooking of charlotte (cake), provided with 2 handles."@en .

gpc:30018081 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "ROUND FLUTED OR STRAIGHT TART MOLD"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a mold intended for the cooking of tarts with fluted or straight edges. The bottom of which is knockdown or not,"@en .

gpc:30018082 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "ROUND PASTRY MOLD (NON DISPOSABLE)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a mold used for the cooking of manqu&#233; cakes, of cylindrical shape with slightly conical edges."@en .

gpc:30018083 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SAVARIN MOLD (NON DISPOSABLE)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of non-disposable mold used for the cooking of savarins cakes."@en .

gpc:30018084 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SOUFFLE DISH (NON DISPOSABLE)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a cooking dish used for cooking souffle."@en .

gpc:30018085 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SOUFFLE MOLD (NON DISPOSABLE)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of non disposable mold used for the cooking of souffle."@en .

gpc:30018086 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "TAJINE POT (NON POWERED)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe the traditional pottery used to cook tajine, consisting of two parts: a circular base unit that is flat with low sides and a large cone- or dome-shaped cover that sits on the base during cooking."@en .

gpc:30018087 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "TARTELETS MOLD (NON DISPOSABLE)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of non disposable mold used for the cooking of tartelets."@en .

gpc:30018088 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "TERRINE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a cooking dish with vertical sides and a tightly fitting lid, generally rectangular or oval, used to cook terrine."@en .

gpc:30018089 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "THEMATICAL MOLD (NON DISPOSABLE)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of non-disposable mold used for the cooking of cake which shape can represents either humans, animals plants or objects."@en .

gpc:30018090 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "COOKING BASKET"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe products that can be described as a sieve-like metal recipient, perforated on the bottom and sides, that can be inserted in a cooking utensil."@en .

gpc:30018091 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PRESSURE COOKER BASKET"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe products that can be described as a perforated recipient intended to be placed in a pressure cooker for the cooking of foods under pressure. It is usually equipped with a folding handle.&#160;"@en .

gpc:30018092 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CHEESE FONDUE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe products that enable the preparation and serving of a cheese-based fondue."@en .

gpc:30018093 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CHINESE FONDUE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe all products that enable the preparation and serving of a stock-based fondue."@en .

gpc:30018094 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CHOCOLATE FONDUE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe all products that enable the preparation and serving of an chocolate-based fondue."@en .

gpc:30018095 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "MEAT FONDUE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe products that enable the preparation and serving of an oil-based fondue."@en .

gpc:30018096 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "FONDUE BURNER"@en .

gpc:30018097 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "FONDUE FORK"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of two-pronged, long-handled fork, for holding fondue items (bread, meat etc.) and placing them in the fondue vessel in which they are cooked."@en .

gpc:30018098 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "FONDUE PLATE"@en .

gpc:30018099 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "FONDUE POT"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of earthenware or cast-iron casserole, with a handle, mainly intended for the preparation and serving of fondues."@en .

gpc:30018100 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "FONDUE FUEL"@en .

gpc:30018101 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "ASPARAGUS STEAMER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a set consisting of a saucepan, lid and a perforated strainer-basket and specifically enabling the cooking of asparagus."@en .

gpc:30018102 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BAIN-MARIE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a piece of equipment usually consisting of a pan of water in which another container or containers of food to be cooked is placed within the pan of water."@en .

gpc:30018103 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "COUSCOUSSIER/STEAMER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a traditional double-chambered food steamer used in Berberand Arabic cuisines to cook couscous."@en .

gpc:30018104 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CREPE PAN"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe an utensil with a handle used to cook french crepes."@en .

gpc:30018105 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "DEEP FRYING PAN"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a pan used to cook a bigger quantity of food than in a classical frying pan."@en .

gpc:30018106 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "DEEP SAUCEPAN"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a saucepan deeper than usually, allowing to avoid the overflowing of liquid."@en .

gpc:30018107 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "FISH PAN"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe an oval or rectangular utensil endowed with a handle used to cook fish."@en .

gpc:30018108 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "FISHKETTLE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a long and relatively deep cookware used to cook whole fish typically with an internal tray."@en .

gpc:30018109 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PAELLA PAN"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a relatively high pan to allow cooking of the paella. This pan has two or more handles."@en .

gpc:30018110 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PASTA COOKER BASKET"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of cooking recipient, perforated on the bottom and sides, that can be inserted in a saucepan, specifically to cook pasta."@en .

gpc:30018111 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PASTA COOKER SET"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe products that can be described as a set consisting of a saucepan, a lid and a perforated strainer-basket (specifically called a pasta cooker) and specifically intended for the cooking of pasta."@en .

gpc:30018112 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PASTA POT"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a pot with a specially designed lid used to strain the cooked pasta."@en .

gpc:30018113 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SAUCEPAN"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe an utensil with vertical sides about the same height as their diameter, used for simmering or boiling. Saucepans generally have one long handle. Larger pots of the same shape generally have two handles close to the sides of the pot."@en .

gpc:30018114 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SAUCIER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of cooking recipient enabling the cooking and preparation of a sauce, cream or sabayon."@en .

gpc:30018115 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SAUTE PAN STRAIGHT &amp; CONICAL"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe an utensil used to brown food. Its shape ensures a good evacuation of humidity."@en .

gpc:30018116 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "POLYTETRAFLUOROETHYLENE (PTFE)"@en .

gpc:30018117 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BAYONET CLOSURE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of closure of pressure cooker. To close the lid, it is necessary to put the lid on the tank, then to turn the lid until the arrows drawn on the lid are aligned with arrows drawn on the tank."@en .

gpc:30018118 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PUSH-BUTTON CLOSURE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of closure of pressure cooker. To precede in the closure of the lid while assuring a perfect waterproofness of the device, it is just necessary to put the lid on the tank, and to press the big central button until this one jams."@en .

gpc:30018119 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "RE-ENTRANT LID CLOSURE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of closure of pressure cooker. It is necessary to put the lid on the tank. Then, it is necessary to turn the lid until it jams. It looks like the system with bayonet, with the difference that the lid sits directly on the edges of the tank."@en .

gpc:30018120 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "STIRRUP CLOSURE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of closure of pressure cooker consisting of a button of tightening and a stirrup fixed to the lid. The stirrup is a generally metallic part which crosses all the lid on its width. To close the lid, it is necessary to turn the button of tightening to lower the stirrup until it jams and until it closes the lid against the tank while assuring these two parts to stay stuck the one on the other one."@en .

gpc:30018121 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CAST ALUMINIUM"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Alloy which main constituent is the aluminium, used by molding to obtain cookware products."@en .

gpc:30018122 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "MULTILAYER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Multilayer is a material consisting of a cladding of stainless steel on both sides of an aluminium or copper core in order to conduct the heat across the base of a cookware."@en .

gpc:30018123 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "KITCHEN FUNNEL"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a pipe with a wide conical mouth and a narrow stem. It is used to channel liquid or fine-grained substances into containers with a small opening, in order to avoid spillage. The material should be sturdy enough to withstand the weight of the substance being transferred."@en .

gpc:30018124 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "JAM FUNNEL"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of funnel specifically designed to channel jam into small containers. Its stem is larger than a classical kitchen funnel in order to channel fruit pieces."@en .

gpc:30018125 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PISTON FUNNEL"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe an instrument in the shape of cone endowed with a piston ended with one or several cartridges and a system of closure of the tip to facilitate the dosage and the filling of glass cups, molds, glasses. They are made by a stiff enough material, not to crash under the weight of what we pour."@en .

gpc:30018126 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PRESSURE SYRINGE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe an instrument consisting in a cylinder endowed with a piston, ended with one or several cartridges and a system of closure of the tip to facilitate the dosage and the filling of cakes, glass cups, molds, glasses. They are made by a stiff enough material, not to crash under the weight of what we pour with the exception of the simple funnels."@en .

gpc:30018127 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CONICAL KITCHEN &amp; PASTRY BOWL"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a bowl of flat-bottomed conical shape with edges mainly opened to allow the cleaning, used for the preparation, the mixture or the storage of various food preparations. With the exception of hemispherical kitchen and pasty bowls."@en .

gpc:30018128 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "HEMISPHERICAL KITCHEN &amp; PASTRY BOWL"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe an utensil with a semi-hemispherical shape. It can be provided with a flat base allowing to put it on the kitchen counter. It is used to mix ingredients in the preparation of a recipe."@en .

gpc:30018129 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "JAM PAN"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a kitchen utensil, wide and rather deep provided with handles used for the cooking of jams. It is often made with copper to assure a better distribution of heat and better gelling, and slightly flared form to facilitate the evaporation of the water contained in fruits."@en .

gpc:30018130 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BASTING SPOON"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a long-handled kitchen utensil with a broad hollow section at its end, enabling the collection of cooking juices from meat, fish, etc. that are then poured over the meat or fish to moisten it during cooking."@en .

gpc:30018131 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CITRUS FRUIT KNIFE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a small kitchen knife with a curved, serrated blade enabling the separation of citrus fruit flesh from the skin."@en .

gpc:30018132 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "ICE-CREAM SCOOP"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a kitchen utensil with a broad hollow section attached to a handle that can be used to scoop and form individual balls of ice-cream."@en .

gpc:30018133 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "JULIENNE CUTTER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a kitchen utensil with one or several blades attached to a handle that can be used to cut vegetables into very thin strips."@en .

gpc:30018134 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "KITCHEN BLOWTORCH"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a tool for use in the kitchen equipped with a small gas cylinder, enabling the production of a flame to caramelize the tops of cr&#232;me br&#251;l&#233;es before serving them, or to remove the remains of feathers and wax from poultry after plucking."@en .

gpc:30018135 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PASTRY WHEEL"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a small kitchen utensil with a small serrated wheel attached to a handle that can be used to cut pastry (puff pastry, shortcrust pastry, sable pastry, etc.)."@en .

gpc:30018136 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PIZZA WHEEL"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a kitchen utensil consisting of a sharp rotating metal disk attached to a handle, that can be rolled over pizzas to cut them into portions."@en .

gpc:30018137 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "POTATO FORK"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a kitchen utensil with several sharp prongs attached to a handle enabling the holding of potatoes."@en .

gpc:30018138 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "RAZOR PEELER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a kitchen utensil with a blade attached to a handle that can be used to remove the skin from potatoes and other vegetables."@en .

gpc:30018139 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "RICE SPOON"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of spoon of big volume specially designed to serve the rice, but also the couscous, the polenta, the barley and the spelt."@en .

gpc:30018140 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SPAGHETTI SPOON"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a long-handled kitchen utensil with a wide, hollow serrated scoop at the end, enabling long pasta to be served."@en .

gpc:30018141 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SPATULA SCRAPER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a long-handled kitchen utensil with an end section that is usually rectangular-shaped and made of silicon; used as a scraper, it enables recipients to be completely emptied of their contents."@en .

gpc:30018142 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "ZESTER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a kitchen utensil consisting of a handle with a blade whose special shape enables the removal of the zest of citrus fruits from the rest of the skin in thin strips."@en .

gpc:30018143 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BREAD CUTTER AND BASE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describes a kitchen utensil with a handle and a straight blade notched at the end, fixed to a board, usually wooden, that pivots and enables the cutting of bread."@en .

gpc:30018144 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CARVING FORK"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a kitchen utensil with a handle from which two long metal prongs extend in a U-shape, enabling a large piece of meat to be held in place while it is being carved."@en .

gpc:30018145 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "FROZEN FOOD KNIFE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a knife with long, high-performance blade, suited to cutting frozen products, of a tough, fibrous consistency."@en .

gpc:30018146 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "HAM SLICER KNIFE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a knife with a long, thin, flexible blade for slicing very thin slices of any type of ham (such as cooked, dried or smoked)."@en .

gpc:30018147 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "KITCHEN KNIFE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a small multi-purpose knife with a thin blade. It can be used among other things to peel and cut onions, and other vegetables etc."@en .

gpc:30018148 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "KITCHEN KNIFE BOX SET"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe an assortment of kitchen knives presented in a suitable storage box."@en .

gpc:30018149 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "KNIFE BLOCK SET (WITH KNIVES)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describes a form of storage for knives to be placed on the worktop, consisting of a box without a lid with several notches in which the knives are placed (only their handles being visible). This storage device is accompanied by an assortment of knives."@en .

gpc:30018150 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PARING KNIFE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a small multi-purpose knife with a wide, partially pointed blade. It can be used among other things to chop and slice onions, herbs, etc."@en .

gpc:30018151 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "VEGETABLE PEELER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a small kitchen knife with a cutting blade and a guiding blade enabling the skin of fruit and vegetables to be easily removed."@en .

gpc:30018152 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "FORGED BLADE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a knife which blade is forged from a steel bar, extending into the handle."@en .

gpc:30018153 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SEPARATE BLADE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe knives which blade intended to be attached to a handle."@en .

gpc:30018154 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "MANDOLIN"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a cooking utensil especially designed to slice fruits or vegetables. A mandolin consists of two parallel surfaces. A food item is slid along the adjustable surface until it reaches a blade mounted on the fixed surface, slicing it and letting it fall."@en .

gpc:30018155 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BLADES FOR MANDOLIN"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe the cutting part of a mandolin. With different shapes, the blades allows to make slices, waffle cuts or strips."@en .

gpc:30018156 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PASTA DRYER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a kitchen accessory with a vertical stem fixed to a base, with several horizontal arms on which fresh pasta can be suspended as it is being made, so it can dry before being cooked."@en .

gpc:30018157 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "JAR OPENER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a kitchen utensil that facilitates the opening of containers, usually made of glass, with lids."@en .

gpc:30018158 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CHINOIS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a conical kitchen utensil, perforated with numerous small holes, enabling the filtering of a preparation to remove residues (fibres, small pieces etc.) to obtain a smooth sauce, soup etc."@en .

gpc:30018159 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BREAD CUTTING BOARD"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a non disposable board on which to place bread for cutting."@en .

gpc:30018160 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BREAD CUTTING BOARD WITH CRUMB CATCHER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a non disposable board on which to place bread for cutting, with a crumb catcher."@en .

gpc:30018161 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "POLYURETHANE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Material constituting plastics"@en .

gpc:30018162 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "NOZZLES FOR PASTRY BAGS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe the tip placed at the bottom of a pastry bag, in order to shape the filling extruded from the bag."@en .

gpc:30018163 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SET OF NOZZLES FOR PASTRY BAGS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a set of nozzles for pastry bag, each of them given a different shape to the filling extruded from the bag."@en .

gpc:30018164 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PASTRY RING"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a tool used to shape food such as rice, mashed potato and vegetables for impeccable presentation. The food is placed inside the ring and compressed with a pusher. When the ring is lifted, the food keep its shape. Also used to create elegantly presented desserts such as mousses, cheesecakes and tiramisu."@en .

gpc:30018165 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PUSHER FOR PASTRY RING"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to design the pusher used with pastry rings in order to compress the food placed in the ring."@en .

gpc:30018166 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PASTRY CUTTER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe an hollow utensil whose extremities are sharpened or refined in order to slice biscuits into different shapes (e.g., heart, tree, square, rectangle)."@en .

gpc:30018167 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SILVER PLATED"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a product on which surface is covered which silver, deposited on a conductive surface."@en .

gpc:30018168 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BREAD PLATE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a small-sized plate, which allows every dinner guest to put down the bread during a meal."@en .

gpc:30018169 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "DESSERT PLATE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of plate whose shape is flat, used to eat desserts. Its size is smaller than the dinner plate."@en .

gpc:30018170 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "DINNER PLATE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a flat vessel on which the main dish is served and eaten, larger than a dessert plate, and smaller than a charger."@en .

gpc:30018171 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "OYSTERS PLATE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of plate specially designed to eat oysters, presenting cavities to position the shells of oysters."@en .

gpc:30018172 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PIZZA PLATE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of plate specially designed to eat pizzas. It is totally flat with a very light edge, and of the size of a pizza."@en .

gpc:30018173 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SNAIL PLATE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of plate specially designed to eat snails, presenting cavities to position the shells of snails."@en .

gpc:30018174 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SOUP/SALAD/PASTA PLATE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term describes a type of plate whose hollow shape, used to eat soups, salad or pasta."@en .

gpc:30018175 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "AVOCADO SERVING BOWL"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a piece of vessel used to serve and eat an avocado, the shape of which marries the shape of a avocado sliced in half, in order to facilitate its tasting"@en .

gpc:30018176 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "DESSERT/ICE CREAM BOWLS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a cup with a short stem, generally used to eat ice cream or desserts."@en .

gpc:30018177 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "FINGER BOWL"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a bowl of water used for rinsing one&apos;s fingers after the last course of a formal meal."@en .

gpc:30018178 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "VERRINE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a small, thick-walled container with no base, whose purpose is to hold a solid or liquid dish (starter, main course or dessert) rather than a drink."@en .

gpc:30018179 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SALAD BOWL"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe an individual bowl in which is served the salad, and which is generally put at table next to the main plate."@en .

gpc:30018180 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "DECANTER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container with or without handle, with or without stopper to decanter or serve a large amount of wine, easily and carefully, in small portions."@en .

gpc:30018181 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "LIQUOR DECANTER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container with a stopper to conserve and pour a large amount quantity of specific alcohol (often liquor) and to pour it easily and carefully in small portions."@en .

gpc:30018182 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "WHISKY DECANTER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container with a stopper to conserve and pour a large amount quantity of specific alcohol (often whisky), and to pour it easily and carefully in small portions."@en .

gpc:30018183 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BOROSILICATE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Material which is a glass specialty bearing rather high-temperature."@en .

gpc:30018184 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CRYSTELLINE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Crystelline is a material close to the crystal, but which does not include lead unlike the crystal."@en .

gpc:30018185 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BORDEAUX WINE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container designed for Bordeaux wine tasting."@en .

gpc:30018186 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BURGUNDY WINE GLASS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container designed for Bourgogne wine tasting."@en .

gpc:30018187 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CHAMPAGNE COUPE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a flared shape container with a stem to drink Champagne or sparkling wine."@en .

gpc:30018188 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "ROSE WINE GLASS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container designed for pink wine tasting."@en .

gpc:30018189 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "WATER GLASS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container for receiving water."@en .

gpc:30018190 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "WHITE WINE GLASS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container designed for white wine tasting."@en .

gpc:30018191 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CHOCOLATE POT"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a handled container, with a lid, which serves to contain hot chocolate, and to be able to pour it conveniently."@en .

gpc:30018192 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "FRENCH PRESS CAFETIERE (NON POWERED)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a non-electric powered device intended for the preparation and serving of coffee from previously boiled water. Consists of a central metal stem which has a lid attached to its top and a metal disc with a fine wire mesh on the bottom that acts as a filter."@en .

gpc:30018193 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "MOCHA/MOKA POT"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a metal device intended for the preparation and serving of mocha/moka. Placed on a cooking hob (gas, induction, etc.), these pots use steam pressure to prepare the beverage."@en .

gpc:30018194 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "VACUUM/SIPHON COFFEE MAKERS (NON POWERED)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a non-electric powered device intended for the preparation and serving of coffee. They are composed of two glass globes, attached to a support, one on top of the other, operating on the principle of the expansion and contraction of water vapour."@en .

gpc:30018195 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "COFFEE POT"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container with one handle, with a lid, and which can contain hot coffee and pour easily."@en .

gpc:30018196 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PUMP ACTION COFFEE POT PUMP VACUUM FLASK"@en .

gpc:30018197 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "ICED TEA POT"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a handled container used to keep infused cold beverages, and to be able to conveniently pour it."@en .

gpc:30018199 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SPARE PARTS FOR TEAPOTS AND COFFEE MAKERS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe all parts of teapots or coffee pots likely to require changing in the course of their life cycle, such as filters, filter supports, lids, handles etc.&#160;"@en .

gpc:30018200 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "HIBALL (HIGH BALL) TUMBLER"@en .

gpc:30018201 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "OLD FASHIONED TUMBLER"@en .

gpc:30018202 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "AQUAVIT"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container designed for Aquavit tasting."@en .

gpc:30018203 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "COGNAC/BRANDY GLASS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container with or without stem to drink an alcohol."@en .

gpc:30018204 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "EAU DE VIE GLASS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container designed for eaux de vie tasting."@en .

gpc:30018205 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "GRAPPA GLASS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Included products which are described/observed as a container designed for eaux de vie type Grappa tasting."@en .

gpc:30018206 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "HURRICANE STEM GLASS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container with a stem, whose elongated Tulip shape is recognizable and usually dedicated to the colourful cocktails."@en .

gpc:30018207 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "LIQUEURS GLASS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container designed for liquor tasting."@en .

gpc:30018208 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "MARGARITA GLASS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container with a stem, which the shape of cut at two levels is recognizable and usually dedicated to cocktails."@en .

gpc:30018209 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "MARTINI GLASS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a cone-shaped container traditionally dedicated to martini cocktails."@en .

gpc:30018210 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "RIOJA GLASS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container designed for spanish wines type Rioja tasting."@en .

gpc:30018211 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SHERRY GLASS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container designed for sherry or porto wine tasting."@en .

gpc:30018212 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "VODKA GLASS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container designed for vodka (type of shooter or tube) tasting."@en .

gpc:30018213 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "GLASSES AND DECANTERS DISPLAYER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe an object designed for store, present glasses and decanter."@en .

gpc:30018214 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "GLASSES DISPLAYER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe an object designed for store, present glasses"@en .

gpc:30018215 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "OTHERS SETS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a set of products designed for drink and/or pour a drink."@en .

gpc:30018216 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BEER MUG"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a straight shape container with a handle designed for beer drinking."@en .

gpc:30018217 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BEER GLASS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container designed for beer drinking."@en .

gpc:30018218 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CHALICE/GOBLET GLASS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container flared shaped cut with a stem to drink."@en .

gpc:30018221 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "TULIP GLASS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Included products which are described/observed as elongated tulip shape container designed for beer drinking."@en .

gpc:30018222 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BREAKFAST CUP"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a small open container with one or two handles used for drinking hot beverages or carrying food and drinks."@en .

gpc:30018223 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BROTH CUP"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a small open container with two handles, used for savory liquids."@en .

gpc:30018224 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CHOCOLATE CUP"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a small open container with one or two handles used for drinking hot chocolate."@en .

gpc:30018225 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "COFFEE MOCHA CUP"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a small open container with one or two handles used for drinking coffee mocha."@en .

gpc:30018226 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "COFFEE MOCHA CUP WITH SAUCER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a small open container with one handle&#160; used for drinking coffee mocha, supported with a small plate which can include a depression in the center to hold the cup in place."@en .

gpc:30018227 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "COFFEE MOCHA SAUCER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a small plate which center often contains a depression sized to fit a matching mocha cup. The coffee saucer provides a convenient place for a wet coffee spoon."@en .

gpc:30018228 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "COFFEE/ESPRESSO CUP"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a small container usually with a single handle for drinking coffee or espresso."@en .

gpc:30018229 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "COFFEE/ESPRESSO CUP WITH SAUCER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a small open container with one handle&#160; used for drinking coffee or espresso, supported with a small plate which can include a depression in the center to hold the cup in place."@en .

gpc:30018230 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "COFFEE/ESPRESSO SAUCER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a small plate which center often contains a depression sized to fit a matching coffee/espresso cup. The coffee saucer provides a convenient place for a wet coffee spoon."@en .

gpc:30018231 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "ICE TEA GLASS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a small glass container to drink iced tea.&#160;"@en .

gpc:30018232 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "IRISH COFFEE GLASS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a small glass container to drink Irish coffee.&#160;"@en .

gpc:30018233 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "MAZAGRAN - POTTERY GOBLET"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a kind of glass or cup on a foot, optionally with handle usually used for coffee."@en .

gpc:30018234 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "TEA CUP"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a small container usually with a single handle, for tea, chocolate, herbal teas and infusions."@en .

gpc:30018235 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "TEA CUP WITH SAUCER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a small open container with one handle used for tea or herbal beverages, supported with a small plate which center often contains a depression sized to fit a matching cup."@en .

gpc:30018236 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "TEA SAUCER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a small plate which center often contains a depression sized to fit a matching tea or herbal beverage cup. The coffee saucer provides a convenient place for a damp coffee spoon."@en .

gpc:30018237 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "TRAVEL MUG"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a tall container with a hermetic lid that can be transported."@en .

gpc:30018238 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SUGAR STICKS DISPENSER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container in which you can put caster sugar packed in small sticks.&#160;"@en .

gpc:30018239 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "HAND MILK FOAMER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a device used to froth milk by a manual operation, for the preparation of miscellaneous drinks, in particular cappuccino."@en .

gpc:30018240 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BOTTLE COOLER (NON POWERED)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe an utensil or an accessory used to cool down or keep fresh a bottle that holds a drink."@en .

gpc:30018241 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CHAMPAGNE AND WINE BOTTLE DISPLAY BOWL"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a bowl for cooling multiple bottles of wine or champagne at the same time."@en .

gpc:30018242 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BOTTLE FOIL CUTTER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a product dedicated for cutting the protection foil around the neck of a bottle."@en .

gpc:30018243 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BOTTLE HOLDER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a stand, with or without handle, in which one would put a bottle in order to pour the liquid that it contains."@en .

gpc:30018244 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BOTTLE RACK"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a product dedicated for storing wine bottles."@en .

gpc:30018245 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "OENOLOGY SET"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a set of devices and accessories dedicated to serve or taste wine."@en .

gpc:30018246 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "TASTEVIN"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a device dedicated to suck up wine and then taste it."@en .

gpc:30018247 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "VACUUM WINE SAVER (NON POWERED)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a device that creates vacuum in an opened bottle of wine, by manual pumping (non-electrical)."@en .

gpc:30018248 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "WINE THERMOMETER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a device that can give the temperature of a liquid."@en .

gpc:30018249 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "COASTER (NON DISPOSABLE)"@en .

gpc:30018250 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "COCKTAIL PESTLE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe an utensil dedicated to crush an ingredient during the preparation of a cocktail."@en .

gpc:30018251 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CITRUS REAMER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "A small utensil designed to extract the juice from a lemon or other citrus fruit."@en .

gpc:30018252 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "COCKTAIL SET"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a set of tools and accessories, which are dedicated to be used together in order to make a drink, such as a cocktail."@en .

gpc:30018253 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "COCKTAIL SHAKER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container that is shaken to mix or blend a cocktail."@en .

gpc:30018254 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "COCKTAIL STRAINER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a an accessory dedicated to separate solids from liquids during the preparation of a cocktail."@en .

gpc:30018255 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "DOSAGE AND MEASURE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a device or an accessory that measures the quantity of liquid (or pour a specific quantity of it), such as a jigger."@en .

gpc:30018256 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "GLASS RIMMER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe an accessory dedicated to apply sugar, salt or other ingredient to the rim of a glass."@en .

gpc:30018257 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "ICE BAG"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "Bag used to crush ice."@en .

gpc:30018258 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "ICE CRUSHER (NON POWERED)"@en .

gpc:30018259 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "ICE SCOOP"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a hollow utensil with a handle dedicated to catch/serve crushed ice or ice cubes."@en .

gpc:30018260 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "ICE TONG"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe an utensil dedicated to grab or hold ice cubes."@en .

gpc:30018261 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "MUDDLER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a utensil used to crush and tear ingredients used for a cocktail."@en .

gpc:30018262 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PUNCH BOWL/SANGRIA BOWL"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a large container (bowl) dedicated to serve or present a drink such as a cocktail."@en .

gpc:30018263 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "REUSABLE ICE CUBE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a product that can be frozen and added to a drink to chill without diluting, such as a whiskey stone or wine pearl."@en .

gpc:30018264 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "COOLING SET"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a combination of at least one container and refrigeration module used to maintain cold food temperatures. It is usually a base, one or more eutectic blocks and a tray/dish dedicated to receiving food. This set can also be equipped with a lid and/or a door."@en .

gpc:30018265 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "DOME COVERS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a non-flat lid intended to cover a dish/plate (cheese for example) in order to protect it or to preserve the temperature of the food."@en .

gpc:30018266 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "ISOTHERMAL JUG"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a pouring container closed by a cover whose material has adiabatic properties, i.e. it makes it possible to limit the rate of change of the temperature of the contents, that it is cold or hot by limiting heat transfer."@en .

gpc:30018267 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BUFFET NAME PLATES"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a marker to write information about the name and/or composition of edible items in a buffet."@en .

gpc:30018268 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CEREAL DISPENSER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container to hold cereal on a buffet and serve with a handle for dispensing without damaging food."@en .

gpc:30018269 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CHAFING DISH"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a vessel using a water bath principle to maintain food temperature without altering odor or taste typically used in a buffet."@en .

gpc:30018270 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "GASTRONORM DISHES"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a deep rectangular shaped container that meets the dimensional standards of Gastronorm (also written by GN)."@en .

gpc:30018271 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "JUICE DISPENSER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container to contain and serve fruit juice on a buffet with a tap. Some variants can be refrigerated or electric."@en .

gpc:30018272 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PRESENTATION BASKET"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a deep container with solid or perforated walls, used to present different types of products."@en .

gpc:30018273 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SERVING SPOON REST"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a support for placing a serving spoon (or a ladle) between two uses to avoid placing it on the table/sideboard/work top."@en .

gpc:30018274 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SERVING TONG"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe an utensil to catch and serve food by pinching.&#160;"@en .

gpc:30018275 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BUFFET STAND"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a display on a buffet."@en .

gpc:30018276 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CAKE PLATE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a flat lengthened rectangular dish, mainly used for serving cakes.&#160;"@en .

gpc:30018277 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CAKE TRAY/PIZZA PLATTER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a flat and generally round serving dish, used to present a tart or a pizza on a dinner table."@en .

gpc:30018278 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CHEESE PLATE/CHEESE BOARD"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a flat serving dish used for serving and for cutting cheeses on a dinner table or on a trolley.&#160;"@en .

gpc:30018279 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "FISH PLATE/OVAL PLATE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a large-sized serving dish, specially designed to present&#160; fish on a dinner table. Is generally rather flat and of oval, rectangular shape or evoking the silhouette of a fish.&#160;"@en .

gpc:30018280 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PRESENTATION PLATE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a large-sized flat bowl, specially designed to present the food on a dinner table.&#160;"@en .

gpc:30018281 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SEAFOOD TRAY"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a tray, large-sized, shallow and generally of round or oval shape, used to present seafood on a dinner table or on a buffet.&#160;"@en .

gpc:30018282 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "APPETIZER BOWL"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a deep container designed to serve food at the time of aperitif, biscuits, olives, etc."@en .

gpc:30018283 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BUTTER DISH"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container that can be fitted with a lid used to present/preserve butter."@en .

gpc:30018284 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BUTTER SAUCER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container designed to receive a small amount of butter to display on the table.&#160;"@en .

gpc:30018285 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "COMPOTE DISH/FRUIT BASKET"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a deep dish in the form of a large bowl with solid or perforated walls, with or without a stem, designed to serve compote or present fruit."@en .

gpc:30018286 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "DEEP DISH"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a large-sized deep bowl, specially designed to present the food on a dinner table."@en .

gpc:30018287 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "MILK JUG/CREAM JUG"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container for serving milk or cream."@en .

gpc:30018288 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PICKLE DISH"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe an container generally rectangular or elliptical generally used for serving appetizers, hors d&apos;oeuvres."@en .

gpc:30018289 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SET OF SALAD BOWLS"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a set of salad bowls with different sizes and/or shape."@en .

gpc:30018290 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SOUP TUREEN"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a wide and deep serving vessel, with side handles, often provided with a lid, used to present the soup on a dinner table."@en .

gpc:30018291 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "STAND BOWL"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a deep, one-footed container for presenting and enhancing a selection of products or culinary preparation.&#160;"@en .

gpc:30018293 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BREAD BASKET"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container for presenting multiple pieces/slices of bread on the table."@en .

gpc:30018294 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "STORAGE JAR"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a variable size container with lid, used to store or generally present confectioneries."@en .

gpc:30018295 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "TOAST RACK"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a utensil with dividers (usually vertical) allowing to place several slices of toast without contact between them to remain crispy."@en .

gpc:30018296 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "STEMMED DRINKWARE (DISPOSABLE)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe disposable drinkware that stands on a stem above a base."@en .

gpc:30018297 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "TUMBLERS (DISPOSABLE)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a disposable flat-bottomed drinkware."@en .

gpc:30018298 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SET OF FLATWARE (DISPOSABLE)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a set of different flatware items, for one or more guests."@en .

gpc:30018299 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "ASHTRAYS (DISPOSABLE)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a disposable receptacle for ash from cigarettes and cigars."@en .

gpc:30018300 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "COCKTAIL UMBRELLA (DISPOSABLE)"@en .

gpc:30018301 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SERVING DISH (DISPOSABLE)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a disposable, flat-bottomed, plate used to present and serve the food on a dinner table."@en .

gpc:30018302 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "STICK PICKS (DISPOSABLE)"@en .

gpc:30018303 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "STIRRER (DISPOSABLE)"@en .

gpc:30018305 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "TRIVET"@en .

gpc:30018306 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CRUMB SWEEPER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe an object specially designed to clean the crumbs on a table, during a meal or at the end of a meal."@en .

gpc:30018307 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "JAM JAR"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container specially design for serving jam."@en .

gpc:30018308 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "MUSTARD JAR"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container specially design for serving mustard on a dinner table."@en .

gpc:30018309 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "OIL AND VINEGAR CRUET"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a small flat-bottomed vessel with a narrow neck holding liquid condiments such as oil or vinegar."@en .

gpc:30018310 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "OIL SPRAYER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe an aerosol sprayer used to spray oil on food."@en .

gpc:30018311 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PICKLE JAR"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container specially designed for serving pickles on a dinner table."@en .

gpc:30018312 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PLACE CARD"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe an object indicating what place a guest at an event, such as a wedding or banquet, is assigned to sit.&#160;"@en .

gpc:30018313 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SYRUP/HONEY BOTTLE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a container specially designed for serving honey or syrup on the table."@en .

gpc:30018314 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "COFFEE SPOON"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a small spoon, the size of which is adapted to the size of coffee cups, used to mix the coffee with other ingredients."@en .

gpc:30018315 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "MOCHA SPOON"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a small spoon, the size of which is adapted to the size of demi-tasse, used to mix the mocha. Its size is smaller that the size of a coffee spoon."@en .

gpc:30018316 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SWIZZLE STICK (NON DISPOSABLE)"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a stick used to stir a drink."@en .

gpc:30018317 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "TEASPOON INFUSER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of spoon ending by a ball in sieve, allowing to keep tea leaves during their infusion."@en .

gpc:30018318 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "APPETIZER SPOON"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a kind of spoon, used to taste all the food (mezz&#233;, canap&#233;s, zakuski, antipasti, etc.) which accompanies the ap&#233;ritif."@en .

gpc:30018319 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "JAM SPOON"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of spoon with a very long handle and endowed with a hook halfway up allowing a hanging on the upper edge of a jar of jam."@en .

gpc:30018320 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SODA/SUNDAE SPOON"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of spoon with a long handle used primarily in tall glasses/containers."@en .

gpc:30018321 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "INDIVIDUAL FLATWARE SET"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a set of different flatware items, for one guest."@en .

gpc:30018322 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "ROUND SOUP SPOON"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a table tool used to carry non-solid food to the mouth. It is constituted by a round extremity, and a handle to be easily kept. Mostly used by anglo-saxon countries."@en .

gpc:30018323 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "STEAK KNIFE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of knife with a serrated blade specially designed to cut the meat at the table."@en .

gpc:30018324 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "TABLE FORK"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a table tool allowing to catch food, without touching it directly with fingers. It is constituted by sharp extremities, to seize or collect the food, and of a handle to be easily kept."@en .

gpc:30018325 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "TABLE KNIFE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a table tool with a handle and a cutting edge or blade, used at the dining table."@en .

gpc:30018326 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "TABLE SPOON"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a table tool used to carry non-solid food to the mouth. It is constituted by an oval extremity, and a handle to be easily kept. Mostly used by Latin countries."@en .

gpc:30018327 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "BUTTER SPREADER"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a round ended table tool intended to cut some butter and to spread it."@en .

gpc:30018328 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CHEESE SERVICE KNIFE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of serving knife specially designed and used to cut cheese into slices or cubes."@en .

gpc:30018329 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "FISH SERVING FORK"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of fork with a long handle, specifically designed and used to serve fish, generally used with a fish knife."@en .

gpc:30018330 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "FISH SERVING KNIFE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of serving knife specifically designed and used to serve the fish by separating it from its fish bones."@en .

gpc:30018331 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "ICE CUBE SPOON"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a perforated spoon intended to serve ice cubes."@en .

gpc:30018332 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PIZZA SPATULA"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a flat piece of flatware used to serve pizza slices."@en .

gpc:30018333 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "PUNCH LADLE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a ladle which is used to serve punch."@en .

gpc:30018334 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SALAD SERVING FORK"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a place setting of service used for serving&#160; the green salad, the rice or noodles salads, noodles or other cold food, generally accompanied with a salad spoon, both forming a tong."@en .

gpc:30018335 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SALAD SERVING SET"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a set of table serving tools, including a fork and a spoon of large size used to serve green salad, rice salad, noodles or other cold food, both forming a tong."@en .

gpc:30018336 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SALAD SERVING SPOON"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a place setting of service used for serving&#160; the green salad, the rice or noodles salads, noodles or other cold food, generally accompanied with a salad fork, both forming a tong."@en .

gpc:30018337 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SAUCE SPOON"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a service ladle used to take some sauce and spread it on food."@en .

gpc:30018338 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SERVING FORK"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a fork, which is a flatware product with long handle used for serving food on a dinner table, generally used accompanied with a serving spoon."@en .

gpc:30018339 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SERVING SET"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a set compound of a service fork and a service spoon, which are flatware with long handle used for serving food on a dinner table, both forming a tong."@en .

gpc:30018340 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SERVING SOUP LADLE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of deep spoon specially designed to transfer the soup from a tureen into a plate or a bowl."@en .

gpc:30018341 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SERVING SPOON"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a spoon, which is a flatware product with long handle used for serving food on a dinner table, generally used accompanied with a serving fork."@en .

gpc:30018342 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SUGAR TONG"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of flatware used to pick up sugar cubes."@en .

gpc:30018343 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "TWO-PRONGED SERVING FORK"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a long fork with two teeth used to help in the cut of meats and poultry."@en .

gpc:30018344 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CAVIAR SPOON"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of small spoon used to eat caviar."@en .

gpc:30018345 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "FISH FLATWARE SET"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a set of fish flatware, including forks and knives."@en .

gpc:30018346 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "FISH FORK"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a fork that is intended to be used when eating fish."@en .

gpc:30018347 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "FISH KNIFE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a knife that is intended to be used when eating fish."@en .

gpc:30018348 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "OYSTER FORK"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a fork with two or three short sharp teeth among which one presents an outside cutting edge in order to cut the foot of oysters."@en .

gpc:30018349 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "LOBSTER FORK"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a small hand-piece of flatware, allowing to remove the flesh of shellfish."@en .

gpc:30018350 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SNAIL FORK"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a fork with two small sharp and slightly hooked teeth to get the flesh of the snail out of the shell."@en .

gpc:30018351 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "SNAIL TONG"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a tong specially designed to seize and hold the shell of the cooked snails."@en .

gpc:30018352 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CAKE FORK"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a fork intended for eating cake that has a serrated edge."@en .

gpc:30018353 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "CHEESE FLATWARE SET"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a set of pieces of cheese flatware, including knives and forks."@en .

gpc:30018354 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "MELON/CITRUS FRUIT SPOON"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of small spoon among which the tip or the sides are toothed, with an elongated shape, facilitating the separation of the pulp of the zest of melon/citrus fruits."@en .

gpc:30018355 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "DESSERT FLATWARE SET"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a set of pieces of dessert flatware, including knives, forks and/or spoons."@en .

gpc:30018356 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "DESSERT KNIFE"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a knife intended for use at a dessert table."@en .

gpc:30018357 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "DESSERT SPOON"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a type of spoon used for the tasting of desserts."@en .

gpc:30018358 a gpc:AttributeValue ;
  rdfs:label "DESSERT/SALAD FORK"@en ;
  rdfs:comment "This term is used to describe a fork intended to eat desserts, the cheeses and the sweets, without touching them directly with fingers."@en .

